---
import { DEFAULT_SCENE, demoUrl, SCENES } from "../demo/scenes";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page
  title="SDR-- · patch a radio together"
  description="A software-defined radio application for listening, decoding and recording. Connect a receiver, a channel and a display, on your desk or on a server at the antenna."
  summary="A software-defined radio application for listening, decoding and recording."
>
  <div class="wrap hero">
    <h1>Patch a radio together</h1>
    <p class="lede">Wire a receiver to a channel, and the channel to a speaker, a map or a recorder.
      SDR-- listens, decodes and records, on your desk or on a server at the antenna.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/download.html">Download for macOS, Windows, Linux</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/getting-started/first-receiver.html">Build your first receiver</a>
    </div>
    <p class="cmd"><code>brew tap newspicel/tap</code><br /><code>brew install --cask sdrminusminus</code></p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="scenes" role="tablist" aria-label="Demo">
        {
          SCENES.map((scene) => (
            <button
              type="button"
              role="tab"
              data-scene={scene.id}
              aria-selected={scene.id === DEFAULT_SCENE ? "true" : "false"}
            >
              {scene.label}
            </button>
          ))
        }
        <a class="full" href={demoUrl(DEFAULT_SCENE)}>Full screen</a>
      </div>
      <div class="window">
        <iframe src={demoUrl(DEFAULT_SCENE)} title="SDR-- replaying a recorded session"></iframe>
        <img
          class="still"
          src="/screens/patch.png"
          alt="A patch with a signal generator feeding a scope and three channels, wired to a speaker, a recorder and a network IQ export."
          width="2160"
          height="1350"
        />
      </div>
      <p class="note">The real app, replaying a recorded session. Drag, zoom, and press Play on a
        speaker.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Choose what the signal becomes</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">A channel takes IQ from a radio and gives back something you can use.
      Which output it produces is what makes one channel different from another.</p>

    <div class="outputs">
      <div class="output audio">
        <h3><span class="legend">Audio</span>Voice and music</h3>
        <p>AM, NFM, SSB and CW, broadcast FM in stereo with RDS, and digital voice: DMR, FreeDV,
          D-STAR, System Fusion, NXDN, P25 Phase 1, dPMR and M17.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="output events">
        <h3><span class="legend">Events</span>Messages and positions</h3>
        <p>Aircraft over ADS-B, ACARS, VDL Mode 2 and HFDL. Ships over AIS, NAVTEX and DSC. Pagers
          over POCSAG, FLEX and ERMES. Amateur data: FT8, FT4, WSPR, APRS, RTTY, PSK and CW. ISM
          sensors and radio clocks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="output video">
        <h3><span class="legend">Video</span>Pictures</h3>
        <p>Slow-scan television, amateur television, and DVB-S / S2 digital television.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="output iq">
        <h3><span class="legend">IQ</span>Samples to keep</h3>
        <p>Record the radio, a channel's baseband or its audio, and replay it later. SigMF in and
          out, and live IQ to another program over the network.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="also">
      <div>
        <h3>See the band</h3>
        <p>Spectrum, waterfall, constellation and map displays, with the decoded messages beside
          them.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Find the signal</h3>
        <p>Scanning, signal identification, coherent arrays, direction finding and passive radar.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Drive it from elsewhere</h3>
        <p>REST, WebSocket, MCP, network IQ export and event forwarding to your own tools.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note">Modes range from tested on air to experimental. The
      <a href="/user-guide/channels.html#channel-catalog">channel catalog</a> says which is which,
      mode by mode.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Install it</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">The desktop app runs its own server on a private port. The standalone
      server does the same job on a machine you keep near the antenna, and any browser on your
      network drives it.</p>

    <div class="install">
      <div class="lane">
        <h3>Desktop app</h3>
        <p>macOS <code>.dmg</code>, Windows <code>.msi</code> or <code>.exe</code>, Linux
          <code>.deb</code> or <code>.AppImage</code>.</p>
        <p class="foot"><a href="/download.html">Pick the file for your computer</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="lane">
        <h3>Homebrew</h3>
        <p>The cask installs the app; the formula installs the headless server.</p>
        <pre>brew tap newspicel/tap
brew install --cask sdrminusminus

<span class="p">or, for a server</span>
brew install sdrmm
brew services start sdrmm</pre>
        <p class="foot"><a href="/getting-started/install.html">All install methods, including
          Nix</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="lane">
        <h3>Container</h3>
        <p>Persists its database and recordings in a volume. Pass through the USB group that owns
          your radio.</p>
        <pre>git clone https://github.com/Newspicel/sdrminusminus.git
cd sdrminusminus
docker compose up -d</pre>
        <p class="foot"><a href="/server/deployment.html">Container setup, auth and HTTPS</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note">Then open <code>http://localhost:8080</code>, select your radio on a
      Device node, and tune. The server listens on every interface without authentication by
      default. Set <a href="/server/configuration.html">a token and HTTPS</a> before you put it on
      an untrusted network.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Still being built</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">SDR-- is under active development, and the docs say plainly what is
      tested on air, what is only tested against fixtures, and what is experimental. Bug reports and
      decoder fixtures are both welcome.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Newspicel/sdrminusminus">Source on GitHub</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/development/architecture.html">How it is put together</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .demo {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
    background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 60%, black);
    background-image: radial-gradient(circle, var(--line) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 24px 24px;
    background-position: 12px 12px;
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
  }

  .scenes {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .scenes button {
    height: 30px;
    padding-inline: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--panel);
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .scenes button:hover { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--line-strong); }
  .scenes button[aria-selected="true"] {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 12%, var(--panel));
  }
  .scenes .full { margin-left: auto; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; }

  .window {
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    background: var(--bg);
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    max-height: 82vh;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .window iframe { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; }
  .window .still { display: none; width: 100%; height: auto; }

  .outputs { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .output {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 8px 40px;
    padding: 26px 0 26px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--port);
  }
  .output h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .output h3 .legend { display: block; color: var(--port); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .output p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-dim); max-width: 64ch; }
  .output.audio { --port: var(--audio); }
  .output.events { --port: var(--events); }
  .output.video { --port: var(--video); }
  .output.iq { --port: var(--iq); }

  .also {
    margin-top: 40px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 28px 40px;
  }
  .also h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .also p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 15px; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .scenes { display: none; }
    .window { aspect-ratio: auto; max-height: none; border-color: var(--line); }
    .window iframe { display: none; }
    .window .still { display: block; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .output { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 6px; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { demoUrl } from "../demo/scenes";

  const frame = document.querySelector<HTMLIFrameElement>(".window iframe");
  const full = document.querySelector<HTMLAnchorElement>(".scenes .full");
  const tabs = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".scenes [data-scene]");

  for (const tab of tabs) {
    tab.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const url = demoUrl(tab.dataset.scene ?? "");
      for (const other of tabs) {
        other.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(other === tab));
      }
      if (frame !== null) {
        frame.src = url;
      }
      if (full !== null) {
        full.href = url;
      }
    });
  }
</script>
